---
alwaysApply: true
---

Read the tasks.todo file and follow the tasks.

Only if there is are related tasks in the tasks.todo file, add those tasks to the plan.

The main goal is to take one task (or related tasks) at a time, ask the user questions, make a plan for it, review the plan, ask the user to approve the plan, then implement the task. 

As part of the task implementation you must update the tasks.todo file to reflect the progress of the task.

If you find issues along the way, add them to a debt.todo file. you may need to create this file if it doesn't exist.